From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: AdrielOrihuela <adriel.orihuela.m@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 2 Sep 2026 08:07:01 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] Send every player to the world spawn when asked to

A lobby wants arrivals in one place, and the usual way to get that is a plugin
that teleports the player after they have already loaded in somewhere else.
Ignoring the saved position at the point it is read avoids the visible jump.
The position is only ignored, never removed, so turning the setting off puts
everybody back where they logged out.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

diff --git a/net/minecraft/server/network/config/PrepareSpawnTask.java b/net/minecraft/server/network/config/PrepareSpawnTask.java
index 9fad06eda81b4c2c1889a9cfa7a6948e7ee01862..b9df82e1ed6c646e5af76a019d643eb6aa44a9a9 100644
--- a/net/minecraft/server/network/config/PrepareSpawnTask.java
+++ b/net/minecraft/server/network/config/PrepareSpawnTask.java
@@ -83,8 +83,14 @@ public class PrepareSpawnTask implements ConfigurationTask {
                     invalidPlayerWorld[0] = true;
                 }
             }
-            ServerPlayer.SavedPosition loadedPosition = loadedData.<ServerPlayer.SavedPosition>flatMap(tag -> tag.read(ServerPlayer.SavedPosition.MAP_CODEC))
+            // LegacyFolia start - a lobby puts everybody at the world spawn
+            // The saved position is ignored rather than removed: it stays in the player's data, so
+            // turning the setting off again puts everybody back where they logged out.
+            ServerPlayer.SavedPosition loadedPosition = io.github.adrielorihuela.legacyfolia.world.Lobby.forceWorldSpawn()
+                ? ServerPlayer.SavedPosition.EMPTY
+                : loadedData.<ServerPlayer.SavedPosition>flatMap(tag -> tag.read(ServerPlayer.SavedPosition.MAP_CODEC))
                 .orElse(ServerPlayer.SavedPosition.EMPTY);
+            // LegacyFolia end - a lobby puts everybody at the world spawn
             LevelData.RespawnData respawnData = this.server.getWorldData().overworldData().getRespawnData();
             if (resourceKey == null) { // only run the vanilla logic if we haven't found a world from the bukkit data
                 // Below is the vanilla way of getting the dimension, this is for migration from vanilla servers
